1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
This is CLOSED BOOK,
built for Midnight Korea Hackathon 2026.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:12,000
It proves that an AI release passed a confidential
safety evaluation, without publishing the evaluation itself.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,500
AI red-team suites contain secret prompts,
working exploits, and model outputs.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Publish them, and the test is burned.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,000
Keep them secret, and nobody outside
can verify the safety claim.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
CLOSED BOOK is a third option.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
On the left is the private evaluation.
The evaluator holds it.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Six confidential checks, all passing.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,500
I generate an attestation.

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:44,500
On the right is what the public receives:
a commitment to the exact model build,

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,500
a commitment to the exact test suite,
the release rule, and a pass.

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,000
Not the suite. Not the outputs.
Not the individual results.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now one private check fails.
Secret exfiltration.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Five out of six. I try again.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The attestation is refused.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
And look at what the public learns.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Not which test failed. Not which prompt was used.
Not what the model said.

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
A failed release does not become a proof.

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
This rule lives in a Compact contract on Midnight.

20
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,500
The attest circuit takes the private results
as a witness, and asserts five things.

21
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:33,000
The evaluator is authorized.
The model is the committed build.

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,500
The suite is the committed suite.
The private results meet the threshold.

23
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:41,500
And this release has not been attested before.

24
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:44,000
Only commitments are disclosed.

25
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
This is not only a browser simulation.

26
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
The compiled circuit produced a real zero-knowledge proof,
with Midnight's official proof server and its WASM prover.

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:01,000
When the witness is changed to five out of six,
the constraint system itself rejects it.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
No proof exists.

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
The Preprod deployment scripts
and the network verifier are implemented.

30
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:15,500
I do not claim an on-chain deployment yet,
because the test wallet still needs the faucet step.

31
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:22,000
Demo, local circuit, and network verification
stay separate trust states, by design.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
CLOSED BOOK turns a private evaluation into
a verifiable release claim, without burning the evidence.

33
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
The proof is public.
The evidence isn't.
